<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error. ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255
        characters, which is why the rationale is here.

        ADDED 2026-08-20 (Tranche 2, Workstream A4).
        🔴 THE SHARED RATIONALE FOR ALL FOUR A4 RULES ON THIS OBJECT LIVES IN
        Buyer_Counter_Price_Is_Positive.validationRule-meta.xml. READ IT THERE. It covers: why
        NOT(ISBLANK()) comes first and is not padding; why these are four narrow rules instead
        of the two paired rules the requirements doc enumerated; why there is no
        ISCHANGED/ISNEW guard; the zero row impact measurement; and why no record type test is
        needed on this single module object.

        THIS FIELD SPECIFICALLY: DPEG_Counter_Price__c is DPEG's counter back to the buyer.
        Blank is the normal state, since most offers are never countered. A zero or negative
        counter is a typo or a failed import, never a negotiating position.
    -->
    <fullName>DPEG_Counter_Price_Is_Positive</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks a zero or negative DPEG Counter Price. A blank counter is legitimate and is left alone; only a counter that has been entered is checked. See Buyer_Counter_Price_Is_Positive for the shared A4 rationale on this object.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    NOT(ISBLANK(DPEG_Counter_Price__c)),
    DPEG_Counter_Price__c &lt;= 0
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorMessage>DPEG Counter Price must be greater than zero. Leave it blank if DPEG has not countered this offer; enter the countered amount if it has.</errorMessage>
    <errorDisplayField>DPEG_Counter_Price__c</errorDisplayField>
</ValidationRule>
